@page "/"
@inherits ExpeditionPage
<PageTitle>Interlock Expeditions — A ready adventure for two crews</PageTitle>
<p class="eyebrow">Cooperative play, ready to launch</p><h1>A different card. The same machine.</h1><p>One crew reads the signal manual. The other operates the machine console. Talk to each other, guide a trolley, balance the freight and get both terminals ready before the clock runs out.</p>
<div class="toolbar"><a class="button primary" href="/host">Host a ready expedition</a><a class="button" href="/help">Read the two-minute briefing</a></div>
<div class="steps"><div><strong>01 / OPEN</strong>Choose an authored episode. A free host account keeps your room controls.</div><div><strong>02 / INVITE</strong>Send the room invitation to another device. Guests choose a crew and need no account.</div><div><strong>03 / COOPERATE</strong>Private role cards and shared machine controls make both crews necessary. Speak in person or use your usual call.</div></div>
@if (Status.Length > 0) { <p class="status @(HasError ? "error" : "")" role="status">@Status</p> }
<h2>Ready expeditions</h2><p>No adventure editor or event spreadsheet is needed. Each episode contains six working stations, its own role cards and a complete ending.</p>
<div class="pack-list">@for (var index = 0; index < Episodes.Count; index++) { var episode = Episodes[index]; <article class="pack"><span class="number">EPISODE @((index + 1).ToString("00")) / @episode.Stations STATIONS</span><h3>@episode.Title</h3><p>@episode.Tagline</p><p class="small">Suggested @episode.Minutes minutes · 2 crews · version @episode.Version</p><a class="button primary" href="@("/host?episode=" + Uri.EscapeDataString(episode.Id))">Host this episode</a><details><summary>Story briefing</summary><p>@episode.Introduction</p></details></article> }</div>
<section class="panel"><h2>Bring two devices, not a download</h2><p>The game service remembers the shared room and checks progress. A refreshed page restores your authorized crew. Your host can pause the clock, welcome a late player or replace an invitation. Real network access is required for shared play.</p><p class="small">The fictional episode source is public. Play fair for the puzzle experience; account and room access remain protected separately. No camera, microphone recording, location collection or open chat is used.</p></section>
@code { List<Episode> Episodes = []; protected override Task OnInitializedAsync() => RunAsync(async () => { Episodes = (await Api.EpisodesAsync()).Episodes; }); }
